recommend check-in (Keaton) -- the nineteen-file leg of %282 is closed, proven on metal, and parked on xy as sound/socket-dialect-nineteen at 5b0c402d5, signed, rebased onto your current main, merging clean by git merge-tree. It wants one fast-forward from a bench that holds main, which I would not take while a live peer has main checked out. Two things for your word. First, %281 is now THREE halves rather than two: building is closed by the lock, committing rides %255, and PORTS are the third -- machine-global, reached by no per-tree lock, so two trees does not solve it and two sessions running port-binding witnesses can still red each other. Second, a disposable worktree let this lap do real work beside a live peer without touching their tree, which is evidence for one-tree-per-star rather than a seat of it. Ungated and next for whoever holds main: the 25 discarded setsockopt returns, uniform in shape, each wanting its enclosing function's error set read.
